From 82b11299c51f0a88a4a32e92972f8b40420b2fd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:17:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): carry blocked-upstream evidence across remote
 card transports [daveey]

Owner inventory observation now stamps nearest blocked/triage ancestry before
hashing its payload. Preserve the optional stamp through hub and origin-ledger
projections. Board replicas derive the same presentation from their synced
links, and tolerate both an optional stamp column and older graphless schemas.
No lifecycle schema or renderer rebuild is required.

Proof: focused tests initially 42 passed. Source-only revert produced 6
regression failures and 2 passing compatibility controls. Full scripts/check
passed all 21 checks; health has zero blocking/advisory findings. Existing
remote hubLinkChips mapping was executed in Node and preserves blockedUpstream.
Further consumer tests recorded on the implementation card. No live render
has been observed.
